cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use tok in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "tok: a plain-text language for information-process models"
abstract: >-
  tok is a plain-text language for information-process models. One text file describes a
  BPMN 2.0 process with the DMN decisions it uses, the forms people fill in and the
  parameters needed to simulate it. The tok tools check the model and export BPMN 2.0 XML
  with an automatic diagram layout, SVG, DMN 1.5 and Camunda 8 form files, import BPMN and
  DMN files, evaluate decisions and simulate the process. The engine is written in Rust and
  used from the command line, Python, R, Julia, a language server, an MCP server and a
  browser playground.
authors:
